From b86a07482d5876047632e1a812f1c0f79af50b35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:28:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(drilling): Back bore carries the dwell and feeds out
 at the plunge feed

The drill generator forced the dwell of a Back bore (G89) hole to 0, so
the user's dwell never reached the cycle record or a post. It also fed
out at the cutting feed, while the canned word has one F (the plunge
feed) for both directions: the CL chain disagreed with what the control
runs.

The cycle record now carries the dwell, and the chain feeds out at the
feed it fed in at, as the Ream cycle does. The posts already write their
own P unit for G89, or refuse by name.

Pinned by back_bore_carries_the_dwell and
back_bore_feeds_in_and_out_at_the_plunge_feed (camcraft-motion lib).

Fixes #1480

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
